     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "I've marked the run as anomalous and asked for a human to check it.\n\n- **What changed:** since growth started, tube pressure has risen from 2.92 to 3.19 Torr, about 9%, and the rise is getting faster.\n- **What stayed normal:** argon flow held at about 100 sccm, and temperature stayed on the 750 °C setpoint with steady heater power. So the change isn't caused by the flow or the heating.\n- **Likely causes:** either the exhaust is getting blocked or air is leaking in through a seal. I can't tell which, because this furnace has no exhaust O2 sensor, and the growth stage needs one to confirm the gas in the tube is clean.\n- **Growth result:** no characterization of the sample exists yet. If a leak is letting air in, any result from this run shouldn't count as evidence about the recipe.\n- **How to tell which it is:** take an O2 reading at the exhaust, or turn the flow off and watch how fast pressure rises. It would also help to have normal-run pressure ranges to compare against."
     }
    ],
